// Title: Potential EACore.DLL Sideloading
// Sigma ID: edd3ddc3-386f-4ba5-9ada-4376b2cfa7b5
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-08-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of "EACore.dll"
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://research.checkpoint.com/2023/beyond-the-horizon-traveling-the-world-on-camaro-dragons-usb-flash-drives/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_eacore.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\EACore.dll" and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "C:\\Program Files\\Electronic Arts\\EA Desktop\\" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\EACoreServer.exe") and FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Electronic Arts\\EA Desktop\\")))
